  "title": "Amílcar Cabral",
  "summary": "Amílcar Cabral, born in Bafatá, Portuguese Guinea, in 1924, founded the PAIGC and led its struggle against Portuguese rule in Guinea-Bissau and Cape Verde. The PAIGC launched an armed campaign in 1963. Cabral was assassinated in Conakry on 20 January 1973, the year Guinea-Bissau declared independence.",
